      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Merkel cell carcinoma (MCC) is a rare aggressive neuroendocrine carcinoma of the skin that shows locoregional and distant metastasis. Metastasis of MCC to body cavity effusion is extremely rare; only three cases had been reported so far. Metastatic MCC in effusion cytology shows small blue round cells with fine stippled chromatin like other small blue round cell tumors such as small cell lung carcinoma or lymphoma. The diagnosis of metastatic MCC could give patients good chances to get recently advanced therapeutic options. Here, we present a case of metastatic MCC to pleural effusion with characteristic single file-like pattern."},
